---
layout: page.njk
title: "Impressum"
description: "Legal notice for the DevFest Berlin 2026 website."
permalink: /impressum/
---
{% from "partials/legal.njk" import filled, contactLink %}
{% set legal = site.legal %}

<h2>Provider</h2>
<p>
    Information according to § 5 DDG (Digitale-Dienste-Gesetz):
</p>
<p>
    {{ filled(legal.entityName, "Association name") }}<br>
    {{ filled(legal.street, "Street and number") }}<br>
    {{ filled(legal.postalCode, "Postal code") }} {{ filled(legal.city, "City") }}<br>
    {{ filled(legal.country, "Country") }}
</p>

<h2>Represented by</h2>
<p>{{ filled(legal.representedBy, "Board members (Vorstand)") }}</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
    Email: {{ contactLink(site.contactEmail) }}<br>
    Phone: {{ filled(legal.phone, "Phone number") }}
</p>

<h2>Register entry</h2>
<p>
    Vereinsregister, {{ filled(legal.registerCourt, "Register court") }}<br>
    Register number: {{ filled(legal.registerNumber, "Register number") }}
</p>

{% if legal.vatId %}
<h2>VAT ID</h2>
<p>VAT identification number according to § 27a UStG: {{ legal.vatId }}</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Responsible for the content</h2>
<p>
    According to § 18 (2) MStV:<br>
    {{ filled(legal.contentResponsible, "Name") }}, address as above
</p>

<h2>About this event</h2>
<p>
    DevFest Berlin 2026 is organized by volunteers from Berlin's developer communities.
    It is a community event and is not organized by Google.
</p>

<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
<p>
    This site links to external websites such as Meetup, LinkedIn, X, Google Forms and the ticket and
    speaker platforms. Their operators are responsible for their content. We checked the linked pages
    when we added the links and found nothing unlawful. If you notice a problem with a link, please tell us
    and we will remove it.
</p>
